# Secrets
.env
.env.*

# ...but the template listing which variables exist (no values) is committed,
# since a fresh clone otherwise has no way to discover them.
!.env.example

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/
venv/

# Data — large files excluded from git.
# Note: the directory contents are globbed rather than the directory itself,
# because git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
data/processed/*
data/index/
data/models/

# ...but the spell dictionary is a small build input the API image needs.
# Without it, spell correction silently falls back to a generic English
# wordlist and loses every book title/author term.
!data/processed/corpus_dictionary.txt

# Keep eval dataset (small, curated)
!data/eval/
data/eval/results.json

# IDE / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Node (web frontend)
web/node_modules/
web/.next/

# Notebooks — checkpoints
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Eval v2. Ship the evidence behind the README numbers -- the query set, the
# relevance labels, the pooled candidates, and the computed metrics -- so the
# results are auditable and the pipeline can be re-run from CI without paying
# to re-judge.
#
# Artifacts are corpus-scoped: unsuffixed names are the current corpus, and a
# `.v1-openlibrary` suffix marks the superseded OpenLibrary run. Eval fixtures
# are coupled to the corpus they were built against -- gold ids from one corpus
# have 0% overlap with the other -- so these are archived side by side rather
# than overwritten. Globs below keep both generations tracked.
data/eval/v2/*
!data/eval/v2/queries_grounded*.json
!data/eval/v2/judgments*.json
!data/eval/v2/results*.json
!data/eval/v2/human*.json

# The pooled candidate set (~3.7MB). Regenerable via `--step pool`, but the
# threshold-sensitivity report needs it to compute how many pool documents
# qualify as relevant at each grade, and a GitHub runner has no other way to
# obtain it. Tracking it is what lets the whole eval run remotely.
!data/eval/v2/pooled*.json

# The ranked lists each mode produced are the one part of the eval that cannot
# be recovered offline: the pool and the judgments are stored, but the ordering
# is not, and it disappears the moment the corpus is reindexed. Committing it
# (107KB) keeps the v1 threshold-sensitivity numbers verifiable afterwards.
!data/eval/v2/rankings*.json
!data/eval/v2/threshold_sensitivity*.json

# Local scratch file holding an Azure storage connection string (account key) - never commit
.storage_cs.tmp

